      "Before the tragic fall of humanity in Eden, the Creator stamped His divine image upon man and issued the eternal charter of purpose in Genesis 1:28: 'Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it: and have dominion.' That mandate was not an external suggestion; it was an innate spiritual coding—the seed of the King's dominion woven into the very fabric of human design. Even though sin distorted that original glory, the redemptive work of Christ on Calvary has completely restored the believer to the lineage of royalty. When you surrendered your life to Jesus, you did not merely join a religious group; you received the very life, nature, and Spirit of the Living God.",
