      "Deuteronomy 28 contains one of the most chilling, eye-opening warnings in all of sacred scripture regarding the spiritual atmosphere of service. Verses 47 and 48 reveal that all the devastating curses of defeat, poverty, sickness, and captivity did not come upon Israel simply because they stopped praying or attending the temple. The judgment fell upon them 'because thou servedst not the LORD thy God with joyfulness, and with gladness of heart, for the abundance of all things.' God does not merely look at what you do with your hands; He scrutinizes the posture and mood of your heart while you do it. Service rendered in bitterness, grumbling, and resentment is an offense to heaven.",
